Copyright (c) 2026 LMA contributors. MIT for the converter and preparation tools.

The nine ONNX files contain architecture, standard operators, external parameter
descriptors and explicitly audited mathematical constants. They contain no
inline learned tensors. 138 external initializer records map to 132 original
decoder tensors and two learned statistics vectors. The learned timestep scale
is also read from the user's checkpoint, never substituted with a code constant.

Architecture graphs are derived from Lightricks/LTX-Video commit
4b2d053057623ddd4d0a1d3e9cd28890e9ef487f, Apache-2.0. The original Apache-2.0
license is retained in ../ltx098/licenses/Lightricks-Apache-2.0.txt. Source, graph audit and
model terms are recorded in third_party/ltx098-vae-source-lock.json. Model weights
are not distributed here; users acquire their selected assets separately.

The converter reuses ../local_prepare (LMA MIT) and the existing pinned
nlohmann/json MIT header. Python, ONNX and PyTorch are developer-only graph-audit
dependencies, not Android preparation runtime dependencies.
